  "authored_scope": "Random scenes: 22x22 half the time; otherwise each side is drawn from 14..30 (a synthetic extension), and explicit sizes 8..30 are accepted. The background is any colour and is strictly the most frequent. Each scene has 1-4 shapes in distinct colours (2-4 by default). Each shape is a left-right symmetric core, optionally split into two mirrored pieces, plus 0-12 mirror-free stray cells grown next to the core and reaching up to 2 cells outside its box. Every scene has at least one stray. Optional top-bottom symmetric distractor cores carry mostly paired strays, so a horizontal axis keeps all or nearly all cells. Random scenes require a strict unique best vertical axis per colour. Not supported: horizontal or diagonal rules, and deliberately engineered near-tied vertical axes. Fixture replay uses input pictures plus explicit leftmost-best axes, because test 1 colour 3 contains a genuine vertical tie.",
  "authored_constraints": [
    "The background colour differs from all shape colours and strictly outnumbers every shape colour.",
    "Shape colours are distinct, so each colour is exactly one latent group.",
    "Each core is symmetric under x -> w-1-x. Stray cells are never on the axis column and never have a mirror partner in the core or among the strays.",
    "For each colour in a random scene, the intended axis keeps strictly more cells than any other vertical axis, so the output equals the union of the cores.",
    "At least one stray exists, so the output is never the identity.",
    "Shape bounding boxes, including strays, are separated by at least one empty row or column and lie within the grid.",
    "Strays per shape never exceed min(12, max(4, |core|//4)), including paired strays.",
    "Integer controls reject bool and non-int values. distractor_rate must be a real number in 0..1.",
    "Replay axes must be the leftmost best vertical axis for each colour. The replay background must be strictly the most frequent colour, and the replay output must not equal its input."
  ],
